# Git runs hooks through sh, and a CRLF shebang makes the file unrunnable on macOS and
# Linux ("bad interpreter"). Checking out on Windows must not introduce one.
scripts/hooks/* text eol=lf

# Same reason, for the sh scripts CI invokes directly.
scripts/*.sh text eol=lf

# Deliberately not listed: scripts/*.ps1. PowerShell on Windows is conventionally CRLF, and
# tests/test_windows_demo_contract.cpp already normalises line endings when it reads one --
# it asserts what the script does, which has nothing to do with how it is stored. Pinning
# those files here would constrain the artifact to suit a test, which is the wrong way round.
